|~ What is declared under `::tag`, the kind of a tag name: the refusal
   of its constructor, and the verbs that live on a tag name, the
   comparisons of tag names, which compare them by their names in the one
   order, and `manifest`. ~|

:tag/construct
  |~~ Reads a tag name as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/PayloadNotTagError
  |~~ `::tag` reads its payload as the tag name it is; a value's own
      tag is read by `type`.
  ~~|

:tag/PayloadNotTagError/refusesAKeyword
  |~~ A keyword payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(::tag:k !| [type /actualType] | eq [::tag/PayloadNotTagError ::keyword])

:tag/gt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows the name of the tag the call
      gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/gt/ordersByName
  |~~ `::b` follows `::a`. ~~|
  ::law~(::b | gt ::a | eq true)

:tag/gt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/gt/than/NotTagError
  |~~ The value compared is a tag name. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/gt/answer
  |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/gte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows or equals the name of the tag
      the call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/gte/holdsOfItself
  |~~ A tag follows or equals itself. ~~|
  ::law~(::b | gte ::b | eq true)

:tag/gte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/gte/than/NotTagError
  |~~ The value compared is a tag name. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/gte/answer
  |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/lt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes the name of the tag the call
      gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/lt/ordersByName
  |~~ `::a` precedes `::b`. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | lt ::b | eq true)

:tag/lt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/lt/than/NotTagError
  |~~ The value compared is a tag name. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/lt/answer
  |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/lte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes or equals the name of the
      tag the call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/lte/holdsOfItself
  |~~ A tag precedes or equals itself. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | lte ::a | eq true)

:tag/lte/ordersByName
  |~~ `::a` precedes `::b`. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | lte ::b | eq true)

:tag/lte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/lte/than/NotTagError
  |~~ The value compared is a tag name. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/lte/answer
  |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/manifest
  |~~ Asked of a noun, answers the set of the nodes declared one name
      under it, each by its address: ::snippet~(::number | manifest)
      the verbs and the refusals of numbers, ::snippet~(::qlang |
      manifest) the chapters of the language. The laws of a name `laws`
      reads, the kinds of the scope `kinds` lists, and what the reader
      declared `env`; what one node holds the axes read,
      `::vec/count | source`, `| doc`.

      `manifest` is asked of a noun, a tag name in the subject
      position.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/manifest/holdsAVerbOfTheNoun
  |~~ The manifest of numbers holds `add`. ~~|
  ::law~(::number | manifest | has ::number/add)

:tag/manifest/holdsAChapter
  |~~ The manifest of the first page holds its chapter on values. ~~|
  ::law~(::qlang | manifest | has ::qlang/values)

:tag/manifest/holdsTheNamesOfAReader
  |~~ The manifest of a reader's noun holds the names declared under it. ~~|
  ::law~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| | :Box/area ~(1) | ::Box | manifest | eq #[::Box/area])

:tag/manifest/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number is no noun. ~~|
  ::law~(5 | manifest !| [type /actualType] | eq [::tag/manifest/SubjectNotTagError ::number])

:tag/manifest/answer
  |~~ The addresses of the names declared one name under the noun. ~~|
  ::set
